[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    29[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    30[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **The C API has no error-reporting channel at all.** `crc16` is a total
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    31[0m:[38;5;10m[49m function over its declared parameter types: it always executes its two loops
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    32[0m:[38;5;10m[49m and always returns a `tflac_u16`. There is no in-band sentinel, no out-param
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    33[0m:[38;5;10m[49m status, and no way for it to signal rejection. The only conditionals in the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    34[0m:[38;5;10m[49m entire translation unit are the two loop conditions `len >= 8` and `len--`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    35[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    36[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Therefore the rows below are *not* invented error codes. They are the complete
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    37[0m:[38;5;10m[49m set of **boundary / degenerate / hostile inputs the C actually accepts**, each
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    38[0m:[38;5;10m[49m with the exact result the C is obliged to produce. "Expected C result" is the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    39[0m:[38;5;10m[49m observable contract the Rust must match, and each row has a differential test
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    40[0m:[38;5;10m[49m in `tests/differential.rs`. For a function with no error channel, "returns the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    41[0m:[38;5;10m[49m same value instead of trapping/panicking/UB-ing" *is* the error-path contract —
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    42[0m:[38;5;10m[49m and it is exactly where a Rust translation can diverge (Rust panics on
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    43[0m:[38;5;10m[49m arithmetic overflow in debug, on slice index out of range, and on
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    44[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `unreachable_unchecked`, where C silently wraps).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    45[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    46[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Error / boundary surface
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    47[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    48[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | # | function | trigger (the exact invalid input/condition) | expected C result |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    49[0m:[38;5;10m[49m |---|----------|----------------------------------------------|-------------------|
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    50[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | E1 | `crc16` | `len == 0`, `d` = valid pointer | Both loops skipped; returns the seed `crc` **unchanged**, `d` never dereferenced. No error. |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    51[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | E2 | `crc16` | `len == 0`, `d == NULL` | `len >= 8` false and `len--` false, so `d` is never dereferenced → returns seed `crc` unchanged. Must **not** fault or panic. (Rust must not form `d.add(n)` on null.) |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    52[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | E3 | `crc16` | `len == 0`, `d == NULL`, `crc == 0xFFFF` (max seed) | Returns `0xFFFF`. Confirms no seed-dependent path touches `d`. |
