[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     6[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Public entry points (complete set)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     7[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     8[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `grep -nE "^[a-zA-Z_].*\(" c_src/include/lib.h` yields one declaration:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     9[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    10[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```c
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    11[0m:[38;5;10m[49m tflac_u16 crc16(const tflac_u8 *d, tflac_u32 len, tflac_u16 crc16);
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    12[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    13[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    14[0m:[38;5;10m[49m There is **no** convenience/one-shot wrapper layered over a lower-level API —
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    15[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `crc16` *is* the lowest-level entry point and the only one. So "exercise the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    16[0m:[38;5;10m[49m low-level entry points, not just the wrappers" is satisfied by driving `crc16`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    17[0m:[38;5;10m[49m directly through the `.so`, including **incremental/streaming** use (feeding the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    18[0m:[38;5;10m[49m previous return value back in as the seed), which is how a real consumer uses a
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    19[0m:[38;5;10m[49m CRC and which composes the two internal loops in ways a single one-shot call
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    20[0m:[38;5;10m[49m cannot reach.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    21[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    22[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Axes the C code actually distinguishes
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    23[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    24[0m:[38;5;10m[49m There are no runtime flags, modes, `#ifdef`s, or option setters (0 hits for
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    25[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `if`, `switch`, `#if`, `enum` outside the loop conditions). All variability is
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    26[0m:[38;5;10m[49m in the **input shape** and **parameter values**:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    27[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    28[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | axis | values the C treats differently | why (source evidence) |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    29[0m:[38;5;10m[49m |------|--------------------------------|------------------------|
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    30[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | A. `len` vs the 8-byte block loop | `0`; `1..=7` (tail only); `8` (one block, no tail); `9..=15` (block + tail); exact multiples of 8; large non-multiples | `while (len >= 8)` then `while (len--)` — two distinct code paths selected purely by `len` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    31[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | B. `len % 8` | each residue `0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7` | decides how many single-byte tail iterations run after the block loop |
